<title>GREECE: BANK OF GREECE DRAINS 100 BLN DRS AT 11.90 PCT.</title>
<headline>BANK OF GREECE DRAINS 100 BLN DRS AT 11.90 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Greece drained 100 billion drachmas of 14-day funds at 11.90 percent in today's fixed interest rate tender, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;Individual bids were satisfied pro rata on the basis of the ensuing allotment ratio of 35.12 percent,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>A pact of 250 billion drachmas for 14-day funds matured today so that a net amount of about 150 billion drachmas boosted the system's liquidity.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
